From: PwndaWallet <pwndamining@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] basicswap: add the Zephyr (ZEPH) coin module, on the
 per-coin-folder interface layout

Four new files under basicswap/interface/zephyr/ -- __init__.py, chainparams.py,
zephyr.py, core.py -- giving BasicSwap a ZEPHInterface(XMRInterface) and a
ZEPHPrepare(XMRPrepare) provisioning module, on the same per-coin-folder shape
this tree's upstream #532 refactor gave every other coin (see
basicswap/interface/wow/ and basicswap/interface/xmr/, both already in this
tree, used as the direct templates below). This patch adds NO central
registration -- Coins.ZEPH, the chainparams/basicswap.py/prepare.py/run.py
wiring that actually makes the engine construct a ZEPHInterface, is
PWNDA-PATCH-14 (0014-zephyr-registration.patch), which touches the shared
files this patch deliberately does not.

Zephyr is a Monero fork (base v2.3.0) with a Djed-style stablecoin overlay;
everything a swap needs -- key-share split, DLEq, address encoding, lock-tx
publishing -- is inherited unchanged from XMRInterface. The stablecoin overlay
only leaks into the wallet-RPC layer (get_balance's multi-asset balances
array; transfer/transfer_split's required source_asset/destination_asset),
handled by wrapping self.rpc_wallet so every inherited XMRInterface method
keeps working unmodified.

Ported from a proven, tested source rather than written from scratch: REU26's
Zephyr coin-add (github.com/basicswap/basicswap PR #531, branch
add-zephyr-coin, head fa148d0) already re-ported this same interface onto
this exact per-coin-folder layout and validated it end to end --
`basicswap-prepare --withcoins=zephyr --preparebinonly` downloading,
hash-verifying and extracting real zephyrd/zephyr-wallet-rpc binaries, 13/13
changed files compiling, CI-pinned lint clean, `test_other` green. See
ResearchWiki/synthesis/zeph-coin-add-dev-restructure-replan.md (the
authoritative shape for these four files) and
work/forks/basicswap-zephyr/basicswap/interface/zephyr.py (the proven
106-line interface body, pre-#532) in G:\REU26 (read-only reference, not part
of this tree).

zephyr.py's coin_type/ticker_str/COIN/exp/__init__/_wrap_rpc_wallet are
ported verbatim from that source (import lines re-pathed only). Two things
diverge from it, both documented inline where they occur, both because this
patch targets a newer XMRInterface than REU26's source did:

  - depth_spendable() returns 3, not REU26's 10 (itself copied from Monero).
    REU26's own comment on this method warns against exactly what its chosen
    value does ("do not blindly inherit Monero's value - retune it for THIS
    fork's block time"); 3 is this project's own retuning, reasoned inline.
  - the wallet-open retry logic is ported onto `_openWallet`, not the public
    `openWallet` REU26 overrode. The XMRInterface in this tree already splits
    openWallet (an address-cache fast path) from _openWallet (the actual
    open/retry call) -- WOWInterface, already in this tree, follows the same
    split for the same reason. Overriding the public method the way REU26
    did would silently drop the cache fast path for every ZEPH wallet open.

core.py (a new file relative to REU26's own source, which predates #532's
introduction of per-coin core.py/CoinPrepareModule at all -- built following
the replan's Phase 1 step 4, the authoritative shape for this file) is a
ZEPHPrepare(XMRPrepare) supplying getConfigSegment/downloadCore/
verifyCoreSignature/extractCore. Grove itself never runs any of these --
ZEPH is always a remote/host wallet the Rust sidecar leases against a pool
node (grove-expansion-master-plan.md Phase C unit C-RZ), Grove's actual
binary provisioning is Phase A unit A2's own hash-pinned fetch, and
basicswap-prepare is always invoked --nocores for zephyr -- but every
registered coin in this tree fulfils the CoinPrepareModule contract for real
(WOW and XMR both carry working versions here), so these are real,
REU26-modelled implementations rather than raise-on-call placeholders.
getConfigSegment hardcodes manage_daemon/manage_wallet_daemon to False (every
other xmr-family coin here routes them through ctx.should_manage_daemon(...))
because nothing in Grove's deployment ever manages a local ZEPH daemon;
blocks_confirmed is 3, matching XMRPrepare's own default. extractCore is a
real zipfile-based override, not the inherited tar-on-non-Windows default --
REU26's replan flags this explicitly: Zephyr ships a .zip on every platform,
unlike monero/wownero's tar.bz2 on linux, and the inherited
extractCoreByBasename only takes the zip branch when the arch string itself
says win32/win64.

Note on the four hunks below: each carries one more `+` line than the file's
visible line count (e.g. `@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@` for the one-line __init__.py) --
a deliberate trailing blank `+` line, NOT a stray edit. scripts/apply-
engine-patches.mjs's new-file path builds file content by joining each
hunk's added lines with "\n"; that join never appends a FINAL "\n", so
every file it creates comes out missing its trailing newline unless the
hunk's own line list ends in an explicit blank entry (join's own semantics
then place the last "\n" correctly, with no visible blank line in the
result). Verified live against this exact applier: all four files came out
byte-for-byte identical to their source with this padding, and did not
without it. Reported as an applier defect in PwndaWalletVault/log.md
(2026-09-03, unit B-Z1) for a future patch to scripts/apply-engine-
patches.mjs itself -- out of this patch's own scope, which is new files
only. Not `git apply`-safe with this padding (git's own parser would insert
a literal blank line instead of restoring an implicit trailing newline);
this patch's applier is scripts/apply-engine-patches.mjs, not git apply.

Applies to: basicswap v0.18.5 (3859612035f8c4476b5cadedf36b875d2f2def5b)
Marker: PWNDA-PATCH-13
